# .env.example — Smart Roster Management System
# No secrets are needed. This app runs fully client-side:
# open index.html in a browser. There is no backend, no database,
# no login, and no external API call, so there is nothing to put here.
# This file exists only because the assessment submission checklist
# asks for one "if applicable" — for this app, it is not applicable.
# (If the app is later moved to a hosted backend, put its URL / keys
# in a real .env file and never commit that file.)
